and RDS Data metadata","tree":"fee63505191559aaf086849c2211e464ca20646f"}],"cumulative_patch_sha256":"1ad8c0bae6148b43519a39bbb59ae0cd6410eb8ee2a5ad2a3d5cba64eb8e7a10","finding_commits":{"review:5555596450":"a16073ad22b029b79b2b1dcc19e11d127c1bab0a"},"parent":"3e597c69a6f92ab8b07fc791fb11b4f34adba59f","patch_sha256":"1ad8c0bae6148b43519a39bbb59ae0cd6410eb8ee2a5ad2a3d5cba64eb8e7a10","tree":"fee63505191559aaf086849c2211e464ca20646f"},"dispositions":{"findings":[{"analysis":"Registered the existing aws-sdk-1.11:library:testSecretsManager and aws-sdk-2.2:library:testRdsData collection tasks alongside their experimental variants, without adding metadataConfig overrides. Executing all four suites with collectMetadata=true confirmed that aws.secretsmanager.secret.arn and the RDS Data SQL attributes now appear under when: default as well as the experimental builder label. All 18 test cases passed with no skipped cases. The review body's three previously resolved items remain addressed in the frozen head.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"review:5555596450"}],"input_identity":{},"outcome":"fixes","request_digest":"5b8ea8c07ea722ec76670c73d16c326bd4c0e2194b51c7789dccc25701e411e5","schema":2},"download_sha256":"dcce8bb25c7e4fd0c4041115d34c64230608c90a04f5ecdf4192a200566d67ea","frozen_sha":"3e597c69a6f92ab8b07fc791fb11b4f34adba59f","pr":20649,"publication_eligible":false,"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","request_digest":"5b8ea8c07ea722ec76670c73d16c326bd4c0e2194b51c7789dccc25701e411e5","request_id":"ee53e2bc6279488abb6354343c4c2878","run_attempt":1,"run_id":38998405205,"schema":2,"scope":"Structural/Git verification only. No target code or tests are executed.","server_artifact_digest":"sha256:dcce8bb25c7e4fd0c4041115d34c64230608c90a04f5ecdf4192a200566d67ea","verification":"verified","verification_run":{"attempt":1,"id":38999609478},"workflow_revision":"d24780fc2512e60cf9785c88eed4b4abd8a29158"},"request":{"authorized_actor_id":218610,"baseline_review_ids":[5550480996,5552333641,5552569436,5552994741,5554798626,5554906168,5555042038,5555095325,5555420571,5555442787,5555571501,5555596450],"budgets":{"max_iterations":5,"propagation_seconds":120,"retention_days":14,"worker_timeout_minutes":30},"commit_author":{"id":218610,"login":"trask"},"findings":[{"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### \ud83d\udd35 Needs a closer look\n\nMissing baseline collection tasks leave default Secrets Manager and RDS Data telemetry documented only under experimental profiles.\n\n**No open issues** \ud83c\udf89\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>1 previously missed issue</strong></summary>\n\nIn code that hasn't changed since last review\n\n<details>\n<summary><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> Register baseline Secrets Manager and RDS Data test tasks</summary>\n\n`.github/\u200bscripts/\u200binstrumentations.sh:64`\n\n[Testing] Collect the baseline `aws-sdk:aws-sdk-1.11:library:testSecretsManager` and `aws-sdk:aws-sdk-2.2:library:testRdsData` tasks alongside their experimental variants. Secrets Manager emits `aws.secretsmanager.secret.arn` by default, and RDS Data emits SQL attributes such as `db.query.text` and `db.query.summary` by default. No registered baseline task exercises these suites, so the new collection records those attributes only under the experimental builder label. Register both baseline tasks with `metadataConfig` unset, following `instrumentation-docs/readme.md:13-14,61-67`.\n</details>\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>3 resolved since last review</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Include default-propagator SQS error test in AWS 2.2 profile](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20649#discussion_r4300806045)\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Exclude SqsProcessMetricsIsolationTest from collection variant](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20649#discussion_r4300806028)\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Include SQS error test in AWS 1.11 collection profile](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20649#discussion_r4300806011)\n</details>\n\n<sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub>","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5555596450","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5555596450}],"frozen_at":1792207193,"frozen_at_iso":"2026-10-17T03:19:53Z","frozen_sha":"3e597c69a6f92ab8b07fc791fb11b4f34adba59f","head_ref":"copilot/exception-log-metadata-collection","head_repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","head_repo_id":210933087,"input_mode":"direct","launch_run":{"actor_id":218610,"attempt":1,"id":38998350012},"loop_kind":"copilot_review","metadata":{"body":"<!--\nCHANGELOG.md is generated from merged pull requests. Do not add an entry unless this PR introduces\na deprecation or breaking change.\n-->\n\nCollect exception-log metadata for AWS SDK 1.11, AWS SDK 2.2, and OkHttp 3.0.\n\nOrganize AWS library tests into default and named opt-in profiles corresponding to the javaagent variants. Test selection stays fixed when metadata collection is enabled.\n\nLabel programmatically configured library profiles with builder calls, not agent properties that do not configure the library. Keep genuine shared properties such as `otel.semconv.exception.signal.preview=logs` as property conditions, and document this distinction in collection and agent guidance.\n\nFor OkHttp, register the baseline exception-log task without adding equivalent library-version variants or `logs/dup` collection.","title":"Collect exception-log metadata for AWS SDK and OkHttp"},"mode":"publish","pr":20649,"pr_author_id":198982749,"protocol":"git-candidate-v1","publication":{"auth_mode":"fine_grained_pat","authorized_actor_id":218610,"authorized_at":1792207195,"generation":2,"max_pipelines":5,"phase":"0f23a4cb29a944c08b5e8d73bcdaec33","profile":"git-candidate-v1","required_checks":[]},"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","repo_id":210933087,"request_id":"ee53e2bc6279488abb6354343c4c2878","schema":2,"source_private":false,"target_private":false,"workflow_ref":"review-loop-revisions/d24780fc2512